{"name":"Fudge Truffle","hex":"#604a3f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fudge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of very sweet candy or confection, usually made from sugar, butter, and milk or cream.","Chocolate fudge."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To try to avoid giving a direct answer.","To alter something from its true state, as to hide a flaw or uncertainty, deliberately but not necessarily dishonestly or immorally."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fudge"},{"term":"truffle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various edible fungi, of the genus Tuber, that grow in the soil in southern Europe; the earthnut.","Ellipsis of chocolate truffle (“creamy chocolate confection, in the form of a ball, covered with cocoa powder”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fudge","blocks":[{"text":"Fudge is a confection made by mixing sugar, butter, and milk. Modern fudge has its origins in the 19th century United States, and became popular in American women's colleges late in the century. Fudge can come in a variety of flavorings depending on the region or country it was made; popular flavors include fruit, nut, chocolate, and caramel. Fudge is often bought as a gift from a gift shop in tourist areas and attractions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Handmade_fruit_fudge_squares.jpg/330px-Handmade_fruit_fudge_squares.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fudge","wikidata":"Q379138"},{"title":"Truffle","blocks":[{"text":"A truffle is the fruiting body of a subterranean ascomycete fungus, one of the species of the genus Tuber. More than one hundred other genera of fungi are classified as truffles including Geopora, Peziza, Choiromyces, and Leucangium. These genera belong to the class Pezizomycetes and the Pezizales order. Several truffle-like basidiomycetes are excluded from Pezizales, including Rhizopogon and Glomus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg/330px-Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truffle","wikidata":"Q2690965"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Karo_Corn_Syrup_fudge_advertisement.png/500px-Karo_Corn_Syrup_fudge_advertisement.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Karo_Corn_Syrup_fudge_advertisement.png/500px-Karo_Corn_Syrup_fudge_advertisement.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"College girls\" making fudge in a 1910 advertisement for corn syrup","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKaro_Corn_Syrup_fudge_advertisement.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/2018_05_Fudge_IMG_1913.JPG/500px-2018_05_Fudge_IMG_1913.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/2018_05_Fudge_IMG_1913.JPG/1280px-2018_05_Fudge_IMG_1913.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/2018_05_Fudge_IMG_1913.JPG/500px-2018_05_Fudge_IMG_1913.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Assorted fudges","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2018_05_Fudge_IMG_1913.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Vegan_Chocolate_Fudge.jpg/250px-Vegan_Chocolate_Fudge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Vegan_Chocolate_Fudge.jpg/500px-Vegan_Chocolate_Fudge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi